                    <AffiliationInfo>
                        <Affiliation>E. Kristin Anderson is a Pushcart Prize nominee and the author of seven chapbooks, including A Guide for the Practical Abductee (Red Bird Chapbooks, 2014), Pray, Pray, Pray: Poems I wrote to Prince in the Middle of the Night (Porkbelly Press, 2015), 17 Days (ELJ Publications, 2015), Acoustic Battery Life (ELJ Publications, 2016), Fire in the Sky (Grey Book Press, 2016), and She Witnesses (dancing girl press and studio, 2016). Her nonfiction anthology, Dear Teen Me, based on the popular Web site of the same name, was published in October 2012 by Zest Books. Her next anthology, Hysteria: Writing the Female Body, is forthcoming from Sable Books. Her poems have been published in many magazines worldwide, including Juked, Hotel Amerika, [PANK], Asimov's Science Fiction, and Cicada. For more information, visit the author's blog: www.ekristinanderson.com. &quot;The Red and the White&quot; © 2017 by E. Kristin Anderson. Contact author: e.kristin.anderson@gmail.com.</Affiliation>
